#%PAM-1.0
# PAM for the Alpine test servers' sshd, which asks its keyboard-interactive questions through it
# (TestServers/README.md):
# - shello: its password;
# - shello-otp: its password, then a one-time code;
# - shello-2fa: a one-time code only, once its key was accepted (sshd_config.two-factor).
# The one-time code is a TOTP code (RFC 6238) of the secret in google_authenticator, which
# pam_google_authenticator shows as it is typed (echo_verification_code). The password method asks
# the same stack, so it signs shello-otp in only with a code too, which it cannot give.
auth     [success=1 default=ignore] pam_succeed_if.so user = shello-2fa quiet
auth     required                   pam_unix.so
auth     [success=1 default=ignore] pam_succeed_if.so user = shello quiet
auth     required                   pam_google_authenticator.so echo_verification_code
account  required                   pam_unix.so
password required                   pam_unix.so
session  required                   pam_unix.so
